OL,3,GNEWSAScientists may have found first
OL,4,Ahint of dark matter
OL,5,
OL,6,FScientists believe they may be one step
OL,7,Fcloser to detecting dark matter for the
OL,8,Ffirst time, but the findings have not
OL,9,Fbeen verified by independent
OL,10,Fresearchers.
OL,12,FScientists from the University of
OL,13,FBristol were part of a two-year study
OL,14,Fto try and measure the invisible
OL,15,Fsubstance thought to make up over 85%
OL,16,Fof the universe.
OL,18,FUsing a sensitive detector in an an
OL,19,Funderground laboratory in the US, the
OL,20,Fresearchers saw an atom and mystery
OL,21,Fparticle colliding.
OL,23,APub: 02-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,343,340,200,160,0,100
